For planning. The national examination numbering scheme takes effect Novemb=
er 1. New examinations are numbered EX-YYYY-NNNNN from a single national se=
quence. The four-digit office series each regional office has run independe=
ntly since 2003 is retired on that date.<br />
<br />
The part that will bite us is that the legacy numbers are not being renumbe=
red. They stay as issued, which means the same four-digit number can identi=
fy more than one examination. I have already had one of these: our 2011-044=
7 is Marchwood Asset Management here in Philadelphia, and Denver's 2011-044=
7 is an advertising and performance-presentation examination of Braxton-Fer=
rer Advisors LLC. Two different registrants, two different years of fieldwo=
rk, one number.<br />
<br />
When you cite a legacy examination in a memorandum, in a referral or to a r=
egistrant, write the office as well as the number. And be careful of the tr=
anspositions - we have 2011-0477 and 2011-0417 in this office alone, and 20=
10-0447 in Boston.<br />
<br />
Rosalind